        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                "word": "hominisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "eefbe39a-f857-4c61-9408-96224d5e41b4",
                        "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hominismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6e09e8d-7213-339e-b59d-3d4efae1c7ed",
                        "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Anthropocentrisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b83a387f-1dd4-4c4d-b241-7f5ddbf439cf",
                                "sense_id": "d6e09e8d-7213-339e-b59d-3d4efae1c7ed",
                                "text": "Dans un sens pareil, mais ayant plus en vue la réalité historique philosophique, parle de l’hominisme chez nous Jilji Jahn (The Silver World, 1936). Jahn appelle hominisme — en évitant le terme plus large (équivoque) d’humanisme — toute idée générale du monde et de la vie qui travaille ou en fait doit travailler avec les moyens de connaissance humains, sans toutefois s'efforcer à les surmonter, et qui conçoit le monde entier, le cosmos, l’universum de toutes les réalités du point de vue de l'homme et de ses intérêts."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0b505833-d0d5-314c-8b81-50822eb62ebe",
                        "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Machisme ; misogynie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f41c95fa-6887-47c7-abc3-2b7a57490321",
                                "sense_id": "0b505833-d0d5-314c-8b81-50822eb62ebe",
                                "text": "« […]. Regardant le monde avec mes yeux de femme, il me paraît évident que la source de tous les maux dont souffre l'humanité, c'est l’hominisme. C'est à l’hominisme que je veux m'en prendre. Toute ma sociologie, toute ma politique se résume dans ce mot “ça manque de femmes !” » Ce qu'elle appelle hominisme n'est pas l'équivalent masculin du féminisme, mais l'oppression spécifique exercée, collectivement ou individuellement par les hommes, sur les femmes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "844ce3b3-e6b6-3079-9e45-274b7c61f5c7",
                        "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Féminisme exacerbé dans lequel la femme voudrait se substituer à l’homme, en en prenant ses caractères."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "pejorative",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cb2a87d-e46d-4326-a110-979f08c5d123",
                                "sense_id": "844ce3b3-e6b6-3079-9e45-274b7c61f5c7",
                                "text": "Cette égalisation compléterait l'œuvre détestable qui s'opère sous nos yeux, et c'est à savoir l'abolition de tout caractère distinctif du sexe. Féminisme tend à devenir synonyme d’ « hominisme ». Point d'indice plus significatif de décadence que cette confusion de l'homme et de la femme dans la société. Quand donc comprendra-t-on que les féministes sont des femmes qui haïssent leur sexe et qui envient le nôtre ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac955f63-ef0c-3d5e-96ba-ba5d3dc08396",
                        "entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mouvement de réflexion et d’action qui prône le renouveau de l’identité masculine et la défense des droits des hommes, en complémentarité avec le féminisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92aed02a-a913-424b-93fd-c03b82c6e880",
                                "sense_id": "ac955f63-ef0c-3d5e-96ba-ba5d3dc08396",
                                "text": "L’hominisme est un mouvement de réflexion et d’action des hommes du début du vingt et unième siècle, concernant d’une part leur identité sexuelle et de genre, d’autre part leurs droits et leurs devoirs dans la société."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b37d0704-97d5-4d04-a88e-36cb216b4bf6",
                        "source_entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "target_lang_word": "masculinism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "masculinism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                        "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ideology of masculinity or of male rights; considered as opposed to feminism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28f75ac1-1e1c-4766-b447-d91b3fc5cc01",
                                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                                "text": "While only women can participate in the building of a feminist culture, without the interference — however well-intentioned — of men, men can facilitate that process by refusing to participate in the old order of masculinism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd775152-fb9f-4534-b65b-d64807bd987a",
                                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                                "text": "[…] the transition to liberal capitalism offers men the opportunity of putting a greatly increased social distance between themselves and women. It is the rise of masculinism which is the primary characteristic of gender relations in Eastern Europe today."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2009b6a8-d8f1-4ec6-8b36-9dee03043129",
                                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                                "text": "[…] a lonely straight male had no equivalently forgiving Theory of Masculinism to help him out of this bind, this key to all misogynies: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "999940a5-019b-4eca-8f3d-13cc3cf4df44",
                                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                                "text": "Each is laden with assumptions and appropriations that, in discursive terms, reinforce a culture of masculinism – the cultural dominance of the male (in the public sphere)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c656b8f4-c369-41a1-a9fc-35eb0d2b74c6",
                                                "sense_id": "85f7eb8b-fceb-3455-ba56-c89d08b9fbc3",
                                                "text": "However, it is possible to examine the broader historical contours of masculinism – the ideology that justifies male domination – and the masculinist institutions that endorse masculinism […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7476b52-2d70-3406-a8e2-da364ab8db38",
                                        "entry_id": "5f15ee11-19f8-301c-a845-871e15dc09fc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mannishness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "994b6d1e-a169-411a-9f58-4737d4d1be9d",
                                                "sense_id": "e7476b52-2d70-3406-a8e2-da364ab8db38",
                                                "text": "The greater part of these various anatomical peculiarities and functional anomalies point, more or less clearly, to the prevalence among inverts of a tendency to infantilism, combined with feminism in men and masculinism in women"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f7fe50d0-907a-4be5-a8ad-cffa6fa6f64c",
                        "source_entry_id": "709aa0ec-98f0-301d-91de-227d833c76db",
                        "target_lang_word": "masculism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "masculism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc660472-f242-3561-95fa-551e1f0657c0",
                                        "entry_id": "3a1edfad-862a-3b52-b2e0-b2f42bb99a30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Advocacy of men's rights."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac203a21-d651-4154-acd8-b97fe3912f93",
                                                "sense_id": "bc660472-f242-3561-95fa-551e1f0657c0",
                                                "text": "[…] proposing the development of a counter corrective movement to be called \"Masculism\" — lady, I thank thee for that word! — a Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Men.\n[…]\nIn his plea for masculism John Macy defies the champions of present-day feminism."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7994e91e-86f6-4538-95ac-6359bb542def",
                                                "sense_id": "bc660472-f242-3561-95fa-551e1f0657c0",
                                                "text": "Unfortunately, masculism also has a tendency to adopt the less constructive traits and tactics of modern feminism, including polarizing rhetoric, exaggerated claims of victimization as the basis of political demands, and the tailoring of facts to fit ideology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "769efcf8-7714-4e0d-8d1b-5938e9c4c395",
                                                "sense_id": "bc660472-f242-3561-95fa-551e1f0657c0",
                                                "text": "I assume, in other words, that a healthy feminism will be promasculist, just as a healthy masculism will be profeminist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67683657-6413-3a5f-ba63-317fa5a67637",
                                        "entry_id": "3a1edfad-862a-3b52-b2e0-b2f42bb99a30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Support for patriarchy / male domination of women; opposition to equality for women; anti-feminism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0dd41d4-1afa-424f-9fde-3fd04e9202de",
                                                "sense_id": "67683657-6413-3a5f-ba63-317fa5a67637",
                                                "text": "The ages of masculism are now drawing to a close. Their dying days are lit up by a final flare of universal violence and despair such as the world has seldom before seen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c5c50ca-2324-4c4b-a018-2a626d7f123b",
                                                "sense_id": "67683657-6413-3a5f-ba63-317fa5a67637",
                                                "text": "Fascism, fully revealed, is the extreme, exquisite expression of masculism, of patriarchy, and thus the natural enemy of feminism, its quintessential opposite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ce6873c-753e-4d4a-a05f-885899d14ea3",
                                                "sense_id": "67683657-6413-3a5f-ba63-317fa5a67637",
                                                "text": "As Brittan (1989:4) has succinctly put it, \"the ideology that justifies and naturalizes male domination\" is \"masculism.\" And masculism is already antisocial because masculism as an ideology universalizes \"man\" as the \"maker\" of history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ce3ac1d-6488-4901-8523-b4af57dc36eb",
                                                "sense_id": "67683657-6413-3a5f-ba63-317fa5a67637",
                                                "text": "Titling a 1914 public lecture series at New York's Astor Hotel, “Studies in Masculism,” she complained that the printer objected to the word and attempted to change it.\nDespite an unfriendly press, she specially targeted \"masculist\" authors and purveyors of negative views of women."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b66dc52-b3b8-3a05-8ef4-1de8de56974f",
                                        "entry_id": "3a1edfad-862a-3b52-b2e0-b2f42bb99a30",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexism in favor of men."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb11d439-62c2-4b77-a580-807bbba2f35f",
                                                "sense_id": "7b66dc52-b3b8-3a05-8ef4-1de8de56974f",
                                                "text": "Masculism, the form of sexism practiced in our culture, has many facets, and we shall explore them in Chapter 2. Here we need only say that masculism is in part the mistaking of male perspectives, beliefs, attitudes, standards, values, and perceptions for all human perceptions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67a9acf7-f858-4b8d-9861-b298a1191ebe",
                                                "sense_id": "7b66dc52-b3b8-3a05-8ef4-1de8de56974f",
                                                "text": "It often takes a crisis of some sort to initiate the difficult but empowering feminist process of renegotiating the masculisms that dominate the discourses of origin, authenticity and belonging in a way that transforms margins into frontiers, lack into (ad)vantage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9888341-4a4e-4d10-9d39-82446fdb5bce",
                                                "sense_id": "7b66dc52-b3b8-3a05-8ef4-1de8de56974f",
                                                "text": "Residual masculism remained quite powerful, and does so to this day. At school, boys continue to command more playground space and teacher attention than do girls."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
